# Cline Rules — The-Art-SampleGod

## Project Overview

- **Name:** The-Art-SampleGod
- **Type:** Windows Sampler Instrument (VST3 + Standalone)
- **Core Tech Stack:** C++20, JUCE 9.0.1, CMake (MSVC 2022 x64 target), PowerShell (`scripts/setup.ps1`, `scripts/build.ps1`).
- **Dependencies:** JUCE is the ONLY third-party dependency (`cmake/JUCE.cmake`). Keep external dependencies to zero unless explicitly requested.

---

## Architectural & Coding Standards

### 1. Dependency Discipline

- Avoid introducing third-party C++ libraries. Rely strictly on standard C++20 and native JUCE modules.
- Keep build scripts portable and focused on MSVC 2022 on Windows.

### 2. Configuration Precedence

Always respect the strict settings precedence:
`Environment Variables > Local .env > User App Data (%APPDATA%\StiffMcGriff\The Art-SampleGod\samplegod.conf) > System Defaults`

### 3. File System & Memory Safety

- Never store application data, temporary caches, or logs inside the repo root directory.
- Use `%APPDATA%\StiffMcGriff\The Art-SampleGod` for library indices, logs, and INI configuration files.
- Maintain real-time audio thread safety: avoid memory allocations, blocking locks, or disk I/O in audio processing callbacks (`processBlock`).

### 4. Repository Cleanliness

- Never check in build outputs (`build/`, `build/win-x64/`), local `.env` files, or binary artifacts.
- When packaging distribution archives, always export clean git-tracked files using `git archive` to prevent leaking uncommitted files or local caches.

---

## Workspace Structure

- `src/` — C++ source files (VST3 / Standalone audio logic, UI components, waveform display, polyphonic voice engine).
- `cmake/` — Build setup scripts (e.g., `cmake/JUCE.cmake`).
- `scripts/` — PowerShell automation scripts (`setup.ps1`, `build.ps1`).
- `docs/` — Core documentation:
  - `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` — Module graph, data flow, blueprints.
  - `docs/BUILD_GUIDE.md` — Full Windows build instructions.
  - `docs/HANDOFF.md` — Maintainer handoff guide.
- `.github/workflows/` — Windows CI build actions (`windows-build.yml`).

---

## Development Workflow Commands

### Setup Environment

```powershell
Copy-Item .env.example .env
.\scripts\setup.ps1
```
